{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"1. **Additional refactoring strategy used**  \nExtracted one cohesive responsibility from `Attributes`: **core attribute storage/query/mutation operations**.  \nI introduced a focused collaborator superclass, `AttributesStorage`, and moved low-level attribute management methods and fields there. `Attributes` now focuses on higher-level concerns (source ranges, iteration/list view, dataset view, HTML serialization, object semantics).\n\n2. **Files changed**  \n- Added [AttributesStorage.java](/data/henrique/langchain_prototype/codex/data/repositories/jsoup/src/main/java/org/jsoup/nodes/AttributesStorage.java)  \n- Updated [Attributes.java](/data/henrique/langchain_prototype/codex/data/repositories/jsoup/src/main/java/org/jsoup/nodes/Attributes.java)\n\n3. **Expected impact on the smell**  \n- `Attributes` now delegates/inherits the storage responsibility instead of directly implementing it.  \n- Moved methods/fields include:\n  - fields: `size`, `keys`, `vals`, constants for capacity and `NotFound`\n  - methods: `get`, `getIgnoreCase`, `add`, `addObject`, `put(String, String)`, `put(String, boolean)`, `putIgnoreCase`, `remove(String)`, `removeIgnoreCase`, `hasKey`, `hasKeyIgnoreCase`, `hasDeclaredValueForKey`, `hasDeclaredValueForKeyIgnoreCase`, `size`, `isEmpty`, `addAll`, `normalize`, `deduplicate`, plus key-index/capacity helpers and `checkNotNull`.\n- `Attributes` was simplified to high-level operations and overrides `remove(int)` only for range bookkeeping before delegating to `super.remove(index)`.\n\n4. **Validation command executed**  \nRan:\n- `mvn -q -Djapicmp.skip=true -Drat.skip=true -Dcheckstyle.skip=true -Dspotbugs.skip=true -Dpmd.skip=true -DskipITs clean verify`  \n  - Result: failed due sandbox socket restrictions in Netty integration tests (`Operation not permitted`), not due compile errors.\n- `mvn -q -DskipTests compile`  \n  - Result: passed.\n\n5. **Remaining risks**  \n- If Designite counts inherited public methods toward `Attributes`, smell reduction may be smaller than expected. If so, next step would be a second focused extraction (likely dataset/view responsibility) into a separate top-level collaborator to reduce methods declared in `Attributes` further.\n- I did not modify unrelated pre-existing workspace changes in other files."}}
